// The `integer` namespace (area 3, question 7; area 19, "Numbers"). Each
// operation is listed in `jadpo-std`'s operation table with the Rust
// function that runs it.
//
// `/` divides two values of the same named type and drops the remainder;
// these operations divide values of different types, or round another
// way, and cover what an operator can't. `T` is a value built on `Int`:
// `min` and `max` take two of one type and give one of them, keeping its
// named type.

public library integer {
    /// `value` without its sign, never below 0.
    function abs(value: Int) -> Int {}

    /// `dividend` divided by `divisor`, rounded as `rounding` says. The
    /// divisor is never zero.
    function divide(dividend: Int, divisor: Int, rounding: Rounding) -> Int {}

    /// `value` rounded to a whole number as `rounding` says.
    function from_decimal(value: Decimal, rounding: Rounding) -> Int {}

    /// The larger of `a` and `b`.
    function max(a: T, b: T) -> T {}

    /// The smaller of `a` and `b`.
    function min(a: T, b: T) -> T {}
}
